		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Line constraint]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=29637#p29637"><![CDATA[
The limits are essentially two (upper and lower) more new constraints along the free axis. You are essentially measuring the *signed* separation of the anchors along this axis. The first two line constraints block the movement entirely while the linear limit allows for some movement. <br><br>Hope that makes sense,<br>-Dirk<br><br>PS<br>The local levers (r1' and r2') are fixed, but r1 = R1 * r1' and r2 = R2 * r2' indeed vary in time since the body can change its orientation.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Thu Jan 10, 2013 9:43 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
