Thanks Dirk. I have the original line constraint working without limits, however I have a question about the behaviour.<br><br>Say that body 2 is at the anchor point and body 1 is the fixed body that the line moves with.<br><br>Is the anchor point supposed to move with body 2 and that r2 stays fixed while r1 changes?<br><br>Given that the definition for one of the constraints is:<br><br>C1 = t.u = 0 where u = x1 + r1 - x2 - r2 and t is the illegal axis of movement<br><br>Performing the time derivate leaves r1 and r2 fixed while x1, x2 and t are changing with time? Thanks for your help.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=9431">c0der</a> — Thu Jan 10, 2013 1:26 pm</p><hr />
