		<link href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=29624#p29624"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Line constraint]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=29624#p29624"><![CDATA[
// Start with position constraint (u is the axis along you measure the separation)<br>C = ( x2 + r2 - x1 - r1 ) * u1 &gt; min_distance<br><br>// Time derivative <br>dC/dt = ( v2 + w2 x r2 - v1 - w1 x r1 ) * u1 + ( x2 + r2 - x1 - r1 ) * ( w1 x u1 ) <br><br>// Define s = ( x2 + r2 - x1 - r1 ). This is the vector from anchor 1 to anchor 2<br><br>// This yields<br>dC/dt = [ v2 + w2 x r2 - v1 - w1 x (r1 + s) ] * u1<br><br>// Identify Jacobian by inspection<br>J = ( -u1 | -(r1 + s) x u1 | u1 | r2 x u1 ) <br><br>This is for a lower limit. For an upper limit simple change the constraint to: C = ( x2 + r2 - x1 - r1 ) * u1 &lt; max_distance<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=14">Dirk Gregorius</a> — Mon Jan 07, 2013 11:33 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
